The question asks whether the body of an arrow function (fn) can consist of multiple expressions in curly braces.

In PHP, arrow functions (fn) are a shorthand for closures. Their body can only consist of a single expression (the expression after the =>). You cannot have curly braces with multiple statements in an arrow function. That would be a regular closure (function keyword).

For example:
- Valid: fn($x) => $x + 1;
- Invalid: fn($x) { return $x + 1; echo "hello"; }

So the statement is False.

